# Terraform Module Standards (AWS)

## File Organization
- `main.tf` — provider requirements + data sources
- `{resource}.tf` — core resources, named by AWS resource type (e.g., `s3_bucket.tf`, `lambda_function.tf`)
- `locals.tf` — name construction, tag merging, computed values
- `variables.tf` — module-specific variables
- `{{COMMON_VARS_FILE}}` — standard cross-module variables
- `outputs.tf` — module outputs
- `versions.tf` — terraform and provider version constraints

## Resource Conventions
- All single resources use identifier `"{{RESOURCE_IDENTIFIER}}"` (e.g., `aws_s3_bucket.default`)
- Map-driven resources use `for_each` with descriptive keys
- Use `count` for boolean on/off features
- Tags: `{{TAG_MERGE_PATTERN}}` — always

## Standard Variables (AWS)
- `prefix` — resource name prefix
- `region` — AWS region (e.g., `us-east-1`)
- `tags` — additional tags (`map(string)`)
- `env_default_tags` — default tags from orchestration layer
- `vpc_id` — VPC to deploy resources into (where applicable)
- `subnet_ids` — subnet IDs for resource placement (where applicable)

